issue-a-form-element-s-aria-labelledby-references-an-id-that-does-not-exist-anywhere-o-02fe86 = A <form> element's aria-labelledby references an id that does not exist anywhere on the page, so no accessible name is computed.
issue-a-form-uses-aria-labelledby-to-point-at-an-element-that-is-not-a-heading-h1-h6-b-dc3688 = A <form> uses aria-labelledby to point at an element that is not a heading (<h1>–<h6>). Best practice is to label a form landmark with the heading that introduces it.
issue-a-form-was-found-that-does-not-contain-an-obvious-submit-control-no-button-type-a95a4f = A <form> was found that does not contain an obvious submit control (no <button type="submit">, <input type="submit">, or <input type="image">). Verify that the form can still be submitted in an accessible way.
issue-a-label-element-exists-but-has-no-for-attribute-it-does-not-implicitly-wrap-a-fi-27b56f = A <label> element exists but has no for attribute. It does not implicitly wrap a field, so the label is not associated with any control.
issue-a-label-element-is-correctly-associated-with-a-form-field-but-the-label-element-d96478 = A <label> element is correctly associated with a form field, but the label element's text content is empty or only whitespace.
issue-a-label-s-for-attribute-points-to-an-id-that-does-not-exist-anywhere-in-the-page-ab4c5b = A <label>'s for attribute points to an id that does not exist anywhere in the page, leaving the label unattached to any field.
issue-a-nav-or-role-navigation-element-appears-inside-another-nav-landmark-nesting-nav-f1d523 = A <nav> (or role="navigation") element appears inside another <nav> landmark. Nesting navigation landmarks creates an ambiguous structure for landmark-by-landmark navigation.
issue-a-nav-or-role-navigation-element-exists-but-its-content-is-only-whitespace-chara-f22b4c = A <nav> (or role="navigation") element exists but its content is only whitespace characters (spaces, tabs, newlines) with no actual links or text.
issue-a-nav-or-role-navigation-element-exists-in-the-dom-but-contains-no-child-element-be00aa = A <nav> (or role="navigation") element exists in the DOM but contains no child elements, no links, and no text content at all.
issue-a-nav-element-on-a-page-that-contains-more-than-one-navigation-landmark-has-no-a-00102e = A <nav> element on a page that contains more than one navigation landmark has no aria-label, aria-labelledby, or other accessible name source to distinguish it from the others.
issue-a-nav-landmark-has-no-aria-label-or-aria-labelledby-if-the-page-has-more-than-on-5c7d71 = A <nav> landmark has no aria-label or aria-labelledby. If the page has more than one nav, users will have trouble distinguishing it.
issue-a-nav-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-navigation-e-g-main-navigatio-6ecfd0 = A <nav> landmark's accessible name contains the word "navigation" (e.g., "Main navigation"). Screen readers already announce the role as "navigation", so this is redundant.
issue-a-section-element-has-no-aria-label-aria-labelledby-or-title-attribute-per-the-a-5be073 = A <section> element has no aria-label, aria-labelledby, or title attribute. Per the ARIA spec, an unlabeled <section> is NOT exposed as a region landmark, so it won't appear in landmark navigation.
issue-a-style-block-was-found-embedded-in-the-page-rather-than-supplied-via-an-externa-59da57 = A <style> block was found embedded in the page rather than supplied via an external stylesheet. Embedded styles cannot be overridden by user style sheets or browser extensions in the same way external CSS can.
issue-a-table-presenting-data-has-no-caption-element-to-describe-what-the-table-contai-f3c448 = A <table> presenting data has no <caption> element to describe what the table contains.
issue-a-table-uses-th-cells-in-its-first-row-instead-of-grouping-them-inside-a-thead-e-7c4fae = A <table> uses <th> cells in its first row instead of grouping them inside a <thead> element. Browsers can still associate headers, but the structure is harder for assistive tech to navigate.
issue-a-th-element-inside-a-data-table-has-no-scope-attribute-leaving-the-relationship-122472 = A <th> element inside a data table has no scope attribute, leaving the relationship between header and data cells ambiguous for screen readers.
issue-a-ul-ol-or-dl-element-carries-an-explicit-role-list-attribute-the-list-role-is-a-1c32be = A <ul>, <ol>, or <dl> element carries an explicit role="list" attribute. The list role is already implicit on <ul>/<ol>, so the attribute is redundant; on <dl> it actively overrides the description-list semantics that pair terms with definitions.
issue-a-ul-ol-or-dl-element-is-present-but-contains-no-li-or-dt-dd-children-empty-list-d93529 = A <ul>, <ol>, or <dl> element is present but contains no <li> (or <dt>/<dd>) children. Empty lists are still announced by screen readers as "list, 0 items".
issue-a-banner-landmark-header-at-top-level-or-role-banner-was-found-whose-aria-label-8b23e5 = A banner landmark (<header> at top level, or role="banner") was found whose aria-label or aria-labelledby value resolves to an empty string.
issue-a-banner-landmark-element-appears-nested-inside-another-landmark-e-g-inside-main-7f9292 = A banner landmark element appears nested inside another landmark (e.g., inside <main>, <nav>, or <aside>), which the ARIA spec disallows.
issue-a-banner-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attributes-set-51d28f = A banner landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set. aria-labelledby wins, but the presence of both indicates conflicting labelling intent.
issue-a-banner-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-banner-e-g-site-banner-scr-7f450a = A banner landmark's accessible name contains the word "banner" (e.g., "Site banner"). Screen readers already announce the role as "banner", so this duplicates information.
issue-a-button-toggles-content-open-closed-or-on-off-but-it-does-not-expose-its-curren-f8d42a = A button toggles content open/closed or on/off, but it does not expose its current state via aria-expanded or aria-pressed.
issue-a-button-s-visible-text-is-a-generic-phrase-like-click-here-submit-ok-or-continu-300bd7 = A button's visible text is a generic phrase like "Click here", "Submit", "OK", or "Continue" with no surrounding context explaining what it does.
issue-a-carousel-or-slider-was-detected-rotating-slides-prev-next-controls-but-it-lack-ef5ce0 = A carousel or slider was detected (rotating slides, prev/next controls), but it lacks role="region" with an accessible name, slide-status announcements, and labelled controls.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-aside-or-role-complementary-was-found-whose-aria-label-9f7782 = A complementary landmark (<aside> or role="complementary") was found whose aria-label or aria-labelledby resolves to an empty string, leaving the landmark unnamed.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attribu-e58b80 = A complementary landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set, even though only one labelling mechanism should be used.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-exists-without-an-aria-label-or-aria-labelledby-if-the-dfabeb = A complementary landmark exists without an aria-label or aria-labelledby. If the page has multiple complementary regions, users won't be able to tell them apart.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-is-nested-inside-another-landmark-element-the-aria-spec-16b28f = A complementary landmark is nested inside another landmark element. The ARIA spec requires complementary regions to sit at the top level of the document.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-complementary-scree-34eb89 = A complementary landmark's accessible name contains the word "complementary". Screen readers already announce the role, so this duplicates information.
issue-a-contentinfo-footer-landmark-has-no-aria-label-or-aria-labelledby-while-usually-82c872 = A contentinfo (footer) landmark has no aria-label or aria-labelledby. While usually there is only one footer, an explicit label still helps screen reader users orient.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-footer-at-top-level-or-role-contentinfo-has-an-aria-label-d354dc = A contentinfo landmark (<footer> at top level, or role="contentinfo") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby that resolves to an empty string.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-appears-nested-inside-another-landmark-e-g-inside-main-or-1fee00 = A contentinfo landmark appears nested inside another landmark (e.g., inside <main> or <nav>). The ARIA spec disallows this — contentinfo must be at the top level.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attribute-31bd98 = A contentinfo landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set. aria-labelledby wins, but the duplication suggests confused authoring.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-contentinfo-screen-re-53e5bc = A contentinfo landmark's accessible name contains the word "contentinfo". Screen readers already announce the role, so this duplicates information and exposes a technical term to users.
issue-a-data-table-has-no-th-elements-or-cells-with-scope-col-so-no-column-header-asso-7d1c3f = A data <table> has no <th> elements (or cells with scope="col"), so no column-header associations are exposed to assistive tech.
issue-a-descendant-element-s-lang-attribute-uses-a-primary-language-subtag-that-is-not-e45dbd = A descendant element's lang attribute uses a primary language subtag that is not a recognised ISO 639 language code.
issue-a-dialog-has-role-dialog-but-lacks-aria-modal-true-some-screen-readers-use-aria-250a9a = A dialog has role="dialog" but lacks aria-modal="true". Some screen readers use aria-modal to keep virtual cursors inside the dialog while it's open.
issue-a-field-is-required-e-g-the-page-submits-an-error-when-it-is-empty-but-the-marku-c04470 = A field is required (e.g., the page submits an error when it is empty), but the markup does not declare it as required via the required attribute, aria-required, or a visible cue.
issue-a-field-s-aria-labelledby-points-to-an-element-that-is-not-a-label-and-not-a-hea-1463d7 = A field's aria-labelledby points to an element that is not a <label> and not a heading-like element (e.g., it points to a <div> with no role), making the labelling source unreliable.
issue-a-field-s-computed-accessible-name-does-not-start-with-the-visible-label-text-vo-e847ca = A field's computed accessible name does not start with the visible label text. Voice-control users who say the visible text may fail to activate the field.
issue-a-focus-outline-is-supplied-via-css-but-no-outline-offset-is-defined-so-the-outl-7491b0 = A focus outline is supplied via CSS but no outline-offset is defined, so the outline may be obscured by the element's own background or border.
issue-a-focus-outline-uses-outline-offset-0-meaning-the-outline-sits-flush-against-the-4b66b6 = A focus outline uses outline-offset: 0, meaning the outline sits flush against the element. Depending on background colours, the outline may visually merge with the element's border.
issue-a-form-field-has-a-simple-label-but-the-surrounding-context-instructions-error-m-6f4e32 = A form field has a simple label, but the surrounding context (instructions, error messages, units) suggests it could benefit from aria-labelledby/aria-describedby to bring in the additional context.
issue-a-form-field-has-an-aria-label-attribute-but-its-value-is-an-empty-string-so-the-fbbade = A form field has an aria-label attribute, but its value is an empty string, so the field has no accessible name even though the attribute is present.
issue-a-form-field-has-an-aria-labelledby-attribute-but-its-value-is-empty-so-no-eleme-a0917e = A form field has an aria-labelledby attribute, but its value is empty, so no element is being referenced for the accessible name.
issue-a-form-field-has-no-label-no-aria-label-and-no-aria-labelledby-its-only-labellin-89fad7 = A form field has no <label>, no aria-label, and no aria-labelledby. Its only labelling source is the placeholder attribute, which disappears when the user starts typing.
issue-a-form-field-has-the-required-attribute-or-aria-required-true-but-no-visible-req-ee08f3 = A form field has the required attribute (or aria-required="true") but no visible "required" indicator near the label, so sighted users do not know the field is mandatory.
issue-a-form-field-uses-aria-label-as-its-accessible-name-even-though-a-visible-label-823248 = A form field uses aria-label as its accessible name even though a visible <label> would be feasible. Visible labels are required for fields that have a visible textual prompt.
issue-a-form-field-s-only-accessible-name-comes-from-its-title-attribute-the-title-att-3beb23 = A form field's only accessible name comes from its title attribute. The title attribute is delivered inconsistently to assistive tech and is not reliable for labelling.
issue-a-form-input-input-textarea-or-select-has-no-associated-label-no-aria-label-and-718d78 = A form input (<input>, <textarea>, or <select>) has no associated <label>, no aria-label, and no aria-labelledby — so screen readers announce only the field type with no purpose information.
issue-a-form-landmark-form-with-an-accessible-name-source-or-role-form-has-an-aria-lab-bbf34b = A form landmark (<form> with an accessible name source, or role="form") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby that resolves to an empty string.
issue-a-form-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attributes-set-o-573904 = A form landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set. Only one labelling method should be used per element.
issue-a-form-landmark-is-labelled-with-aria-label-text-only-visible-to-assistive-tech-c70299 = A form landmark is labelled with aria-label (text only visible to assistive tech) even though a visible heading or label exists nearby that could be used via aria-labelledby instead.
issue-a-form-landmark-s-accessible-name-includes-the-word-form-e-g-contact-form-screen-083cc7 = A form landmark's accessible name includes the word "form" (e.g., "Contact form"). Screen readers already announce the role as "form", so this duplicates information.
issue-a-group-of-related-radio-buttons-or-checkboxes-was-found-but-they-are-not-wrappe-65a215 = A group of related radio buttons or checkboxes was found, but they are not wrapped in a <fieldset> with a <legend> describing the group's purpose.
issue-a-heading-element-h1-h6-was-found-whose-visible-text-is-empty-contains-only-whit-00f9eb = A heading element (<h1>–<h6>) was found whose visible text is empty, contains only whitespace, or contains only non-text characters such as decorative symbols.
issue-a-heading-element-carries-an-id-attribute-which-is-typically-used-as-an-in-page-3efdbb = A heading element carries an id attribute, which is typically used as an in-page anchor target. Verify the id is referenced by working navigation links and that the heading text makes sense as a destination label.
issue-a-heading-element-exists-in-the-dom-but-is-hidden-via-display-none-most-screen-r-2abaa4 = A heading element exists in the DOM but is hidden via display:none. Most screen readers skip display:none content, so the heading does not appear in the headings list.
issue-a-heading-s-computed-accessible-name-after-applying-aria-label-aria-labelledby-e-fac2a6 = A heading's computed accessible name (after applying aria-label, aria-labelledby, etc.) does not include the visible text of the heading, so screen reader users and sighted users perceive a different name.
issue-a-landmark-contains-a-heading-at-the-start-but-the-landmark-s-aria-labelledby-po-b506ad = A landmark contains a heading at the start, but the landmark's aria-labelledby points to a different element instead of using that heading as its label.
issue-a-landmark-contains-a-heading-that-could-naturally-serve-as-its-label-but-the-la-ea31e5 = A landmark contains a heading that could naturally serve as its label, but the landmark has no aria-labelledby pointing to it (and no other accessible name).
issue-a-link-inside-body-text-is-distinguished-from-surrounding-text-by-colour-alone-n-6c282f = A link inside body text is distinguished from surrounding text by colour alone — no underline, weight change, or other non-colour indicator is applied.
issue-a-link-to-a-document-e-g-a-pdf-uses-generic-text-such-as-pdf-download-or-documen-3fe7dc = A link to a document (e.g., a PDF) uses generic text such as "PDF", "download", or "document" without describing the document's contents.
issue-a-link-to-a-downloadable-document-e-g-pdf-docx-xlsx-does-not-indicate-the-file-t-2ddc1c = A link to a downloadable document (e.g., PDF, DOCX, XLSX) does not indicate the file type or file size in its visible text or accessible name.
issue-a-link-uses-target-blank-or-otherwise-opens-in-a-new-tab-window-without-any-text-6314ab = A link uses target="_blank" (or otherwise opens in a new tab/window) without any text, icon, or aria-label indicating that the navigation context will change.
issue-a-link-s-hreflang-attribute-is-present-but-its-value-is-an-empty-string-so-the-l-6736a1 = A link's hreflang attribute is present but its value is an empty string, so the language of the linked resource is not declared.
issue-a-link-s-hreflang-attribute-uses-a-primary-language-subtag-that-is-not-a-recogni-dc5c03 = A link's hreflang attribute uses a primary language subtag that is not a recognised ISO 639 language code.
issue-a-link-s-text-e-g-click-here-more-read-more-does-not-describe-its-destination-or-8a7f04 = A link's text (e.g., "click here", "more", "read more") does not describe its destination or purpose when read out of context, which is how screen reader users typically encounter links.
issue-a-list-ul-ol-is-nested-more-than-3-levels-deep-deeply-nested-lists-are-hard-to-t-690195 = A list (<ul>, <ol>) is nested more than 3 levels deep. Deeply nested lists are hard to track audibly with a screen reader, which announces "list level N" at each step.
issue-a-modal-dialog-does-not-close-when-the-escape-key-is-pressed-breaking-a-fundamen-2a8ae3 = A modal dialog does not close when the Escape key is pressed, breaking a fundamental WCAG keyboard expectation for dismissible overlays.
issue-a-modal-dialog-has-no-mechanism-at-all-to-dismiss-it-no-close-button-no-overlay-c2e606 = A modal dialog has no mechanism at all to dismiss it — no close button, no overlay click handler, and no Escape key support.
issue-a-modal-dialog-overlay-is-showing-but-its-container-is-missing-aria-modal-true-s-eb35ed = A modal dialog overlay is showing but its container is missing aria-modal="true". Some assistive tech may continue to surface background content as a result.
issue-a-modal-or-dialog-is-open-but-has-no-visible-close-control-no-x-button-no-cancel-aea77b = A modal or dialog is open but has no visible close control (no "X" button, no "Cancel", no "Close").
issue-a-modal-dialog-is-open-but-contains-no-focusable-elements-at-all-no-buttons-no-l-5cc67f = A modal/dialog is open but contains no focusable elements at all — no buttons, no links, no inputs. Keyboard users cannot move focus inside the dialog.
issue-a-modal-dialog-is-open-but-its-container-element-has-no-aria-label-aria-labelled-515c6b = A modal/dialog is open but its container element has no aria-label, aria-labelledby, or other source of an accessible name.
issue-a-navigation-landmark-nav-or-role-navigation-has-an-aria-label-or-aria-labelledb-34253e = A navigation landmark (<nav> or role="navigation") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby that resolves to an empty string, so screen readers cannot tell this nav apart from any others.
issue-a-navigation-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attributes-ee0f56 = A navigation landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set. Use only one labelling method per element.
issue-a-navigation-menu-e-g-a-flyout-or-mega-menu-was-detected-without-the-appropriate-1f5bd7 = A navigation menu (e.g., a flyout or mega-menu) was detected without the appropriate ARIA pattern — no role="menu"/role="menuitem" structure and no roving-tabindex keyboard handling.
issue-a-non-interactive-element-e-g-div-span-p-has-tabindex-0-inserting-it-into-the-ta-859b24 = A non-interactive element (e.g., <div>, <span>, <p>) has tabindex="0", inserting it into the tab order even though it has no role, keyboard handlers, or apparent reason to receive focus.
issue-a-piece-of-substantive-page-content-sits-outside-every-landmark-region-banner-na-cf848e = A piece of substantive page content sits outside every landmark region (banner, nav, main, complementary, contentinfo, region, search, form). Users navigating by landmarks will skip past it.
issue-a-region-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attributes-set-3d4d3f = A region landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set. Choose one labelling method, not both.
issue-a-region-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-navigation-e-g-site-naviga-66159d = A region landmark's accessible name contains the word "navigation" (e.g., "Site navigation region"), confusing users about whether this is a region or a nav landmark.
issue-a-setinterval-or-equivalent-on-the-page-fires-more-frequently-than-once-per-seco-b79b5e = A setInterval (or equivalent) on the page fires more frequently than once per second. Rapid updates can interrupt screen reader output and trigger seizures or vestibular reactions.
issue-a-substantial-block-of-body-text-is-rendered-in-italics-italic-body-text-reduces-6530c7 = A substantial block of body text is rendered in italics. Italic body text reduces reading speed, particularly for users with dyslexia or low vision.
issue-a-tab-style-widget-was-identified-visually-but-its-markup-is-missing-role-tablis-8e4a1a = A tab-style widget was identified visually, but its markup is missing role="tablist", role="tab", role="tabpanel", and aria-selected state management.
issue-a-tabindex-attribute-is-set-on-a-non-interactive-element-e-g-div-p-section-witho-5ddb94 = A tabindex attribute is set on a non-interactive element (e.g., <div>, <p>, <section>) without an accompanying role or keyboard handler, so focus lands on an element that does nothing.
issue-ai-flagged-an-unclassified-accessibility-issue-9fc481 = AI flagged an unclassified accessibility issue
issue-an-a-element-is-styled-visually-like-a-button-background-padding-border-radius-b-137227 = An <a> element is styled visually like a button (background, padding, border-radius), but using a link instead of <button> can confuse screen reader and keyboard users who expect Enter vs. Space behaviour.
issue-an-iframe-element-has-no-title-attribute-so-screen-readers-cannot-describe-what-667e67 = An <iframe> element has no title attribute, so screen readers cannot describe what the embedded frame contains.
issue-an-iframe-that-embeds-a-map-e-g-google-maps-has-no-title-attribute-so-assistive-11bd9a = An <iframe> that embeds a map (e.g., Google Maps) has no title attribute, so assistive tech cannot describe the frame's purpose.
issue-an-iframe-that-embeds-a-video-player-e-g-youtube-vimeo-has-no-title-attribute-le-d96d27 = An <iframe> that embeds a video player (e.g., YouTube, Vimeo) has no title attribute, leaving screen reader users without a name for the embedded video.
issue-an-img-element-has-no-alt-attribute-at-all-not-even-alt-so-assistive-tech-announ-3c5227 = An <img> element has no alt attribute at all (not even alt=""), so assistive tech announces something like the filename or simply "image" with no description.
issue-an-img-has-an-alt-attribute-but-its-value-is-only-whitespace-spaces-tabs-or-line-4efe38 = An <img> has an alt attribute, but its value is only whitespace (spaces, tabs, or line breaks). This is not the same as alt="" and may be processed inconsistently by assistive tech.
issue-an-svg-element-marked-with-role-img-was-detected-confirm-that-it-has-an-appropri-fee533 = An <svg> element marked with role="img" was detected. Confirm that it has an appropriate accessible name supplied via aria-label, aria-labelledby, or a child <title> element.
issue-an-html5-video-element-has-no-controls-attribute-and-no-custom-ui-providing-play-18c034 = An HTML5 <video> element has no controls attribute and no custom UI providing play/pause/volume controls.
issue-an-alt-attribute-was-found-on-an-element-that-does-not-support-it-per-html-spec-19f690 = An alt attribute was found on an element that does not support it per HTML spec (such as <div>, <span>, or <a>), where the attribute will be silently ignored.
issue-an-animation-was-detected-whose-properties-large-area-high-contrast-fast-loop-fl-0d7134 = An animation was detected whose properties (large area, high contrast, fast loop, flashing) may pose accessibility concerns such as triggering seizures or vestibular discomfort.
issue-an-element-other-than-html-has-a-lang-attribute-present-but-no-value-lang-which-fab1f3 = An element (other than <html>) has a lang attribute present but no value (lang=""), which leaves the language ambiguous for the nested content.
issue-an-element-behaves-like-a-clickable-control-has-a-click-handler-or-interactive-r-22ac5d = An element behaves like a clickable control (has a click handler or interactive role) but its CSS does not set cursor: pointer, so mouse users get no hover affordance.
issue-an-element-has-a-tabindex-greater-than-0-e-g-tabindex-5-which-overrides-the-natu-cb2670 = An element has a tabindex greater than 0 (e.g., tabindex="5"), which overrides the natural document order and forces a custom tab sequence that almost always breaks somewhere.
issue-an-element-has-a-tabindex-greater-than-10-indicating-a-manually-orchestrated-tab-4ff469 = An element has a tabindex greater than 10, indicating a manually orchestrated tab order. Such sequences are fragile and easy to break when the page changes.
issue-an-element-has-a-title-attribute-but-its-value-is-empty-providing-no-tooltip-or-4879b5 = An element has a title attribute, but its value is empty, providing no tooltip or fallback accessible name.
issue-an-element-has-an-aria-level-attribute-but-no-role-attribute-at-all-aria-level-i-91a892 = An element has an aria-level attribute but no role attribute at all. aria-level is only meaningful when paired with role="heading".
issue-an-element-has-an-aria-level-attribute-set-but-its-role-is-not-heading-and-it-is-f10f73 = An element has an aria-level attribute set, but its role is not "heading" and it is not a native <h1>–<h6>. aria-level only has meaning on heading-role elements.
issue-an-element-has-an-onclick-handler-or-similar-javascript-click-listener-but-no-ro-2eb51f = An element has an onclick handler (or similar JavaScript click listener) but no role, no tabindex, and no keyboard event handlers — so it can be clicked but not activated with a keyboard.
issue-an-element-has-role-heading-but-no-aria-level-attribute-without-aria-level-assis-d15917 = An element has role="heading" but no aria-level attribute. Without aria-level, assistive tech cannot determine the heading's hierarchy level.
issue-an-element-that-is-the-target-of-an-in-page-anchor-link-has-tabindex-set-unneces-d25d09 = An element that is the target of an in-page anchor link has tabindex set unnecessarily. Modern browsers focus anchor targets without tabindex.
issue-an-element-uses-the-title-attribute-as-a-primary-information-channel-title-is-no-571b4b = An element uses the title attribute as a primary information channel. Title is not reliably announced by screen readers and is invisible to touch users — never use it as the only label or instruction.
issue-an-element-with-no-interactive-role-and-no-event-handlers-has-tabindex-0-so-the-7a8491 = An element with no interactive role and no event handlers has tabindex="0", so the keyboard can land on it but cannot trigger any action from it.
issue-an-element-with-role-main-or-a-main-element-exists-but-is-hidden-via-display-non-59fa0b = An element with role="main" or a <main> element exists but is hidden via display:none, visibility:hidden, the hidden attribute, or aria-hidden="true".
issue-an-element-with-role-region-is-missing-an-aria-label-or-aria-labelledby-without-f7b7f7 = An element with role="region" is missing an aria-label or aria-labelledby. Without a label, the region cannot be distinguished in the landmarks list.
issue-an-element-s-aria-level-value-is-outside-the-valid-heading-level-range-values-mu-4bcb00 = An element's aria-level value is outside the valid heading-level range — values must be integers from 1 to 6.
issue-an-element-s-computed-accessible-name-is-generic-e-g-link-button-image-rather-th-d6b9c6 = An element's computed accessible name is generic (e.g., "link", "button", "image") rather than describing the element's specific purpose or destination.
issue-an-element-s-tabindex-attribute-has-a-value-that-is-not-a-valid-integer-e-g-true-d5c211 = An element's tabindex attribute has a value that is not a valid integer (e.g., "true", "none", "0.5", or empty).
issue-an-element-s-visible-text-differs-from-its-aria-label-voice-control-users-typica-2be770 = An element's visible text differs from its aria-label. Voice-control users typically say what they see — if the visible text is not contained in the accessible name, voice commands won't match.
issue-an-hreflang-attribute-was-found-on-an-element-that-is-not-an-a-area-or-link-href-1723cc = An hreflang attribute was found on an element that is not an <a>, <area>, or <link>. hreflang is only meaningful on link elements.
issue-an-image-s-alt-attribute-contains-literal-html-tags-e-g-b-logo-b-alt-is-a-plain-e37901 = An image's alt attribute contains literal HTML tags (e.g., "<b>logo</b>"). Alt is a plain-text attribute — markup is announced verbatim by some screen readers.
issue-an-image-s-alt-text-is-over-150-characters-long-with-no-surrounding-structure-lo-0af1a2 = An image's alt text is over 150 characters long with no surrounding structure. Long alt text is hard to consume in one go via a screen reader.
issue-an-image-s-alt-text-starts-with-phrases-such-as-image-of-picture-of-or-graphic-o-b58c36 = An image's alt text starts with phrases such as "image of", "picture of", or "graphic of". Screen readers already announce the element as an image, so this wording is redundant.
issue-an-inline-svg-element-was-found-in-the-page-inline-svgs-can-be-decorative-inform-e44bbf = An inline <svg> element was found in the page. Inline SVGs can be decorative, informative, or interactive, so each instance needs to be reviewed individually to determine the appropriate accessibility markup.
issue-an-inline-svg-has-no-accessible-name-no-title-child-no-aria-label-and-no-aria-la-e2ea10 = An inline <svg> has no accessible name — no <title> child, no aria-label, and no aria-labelledby — and no role indicating it should be ignored as decorative.
issue-an-interactive-element-button-link-custom-widget-has-no-accessible-name-derivabl-942528 = An interactive element (button, link, custom widget) has no accessible name derivable from visible text, aria-label, aria-labelledby, alt text, or a <title> child.
issue-an-interactive-element-e-g-a-custom-widget-has-a-tabindex-value-inconsistent-wit-6f71c7 = An interactive element (e.g., a custom widget) has a tabindex value inconsistent with its role — for example, tabindex="-1" on something the user is supposed to be able to tab to.
issue-an-interactive-element-e-g-a-link-or-button-has-a-negative-tabindex-such-as-tabi-8e3343 = An interactive element (e.g., a link or button) has a negative tabindex such as tabindex="-1". This is intentional in some patterns (modals, custom widgets) but often signals a mistake.
issue-an-interactive-element-has-a-negative-tabindex-e-g-tabindex-1-which-removes-it-f-925894 = An interactive element has a negative tabindex (e.g., tabindex="-1"), which removes it from the keyboard tab order even though it remains visible and clickable.
issue-an-interactive-element-produces-no-visible-change-when-it-receives-keyboard-focu-9afd1c = An interactive element produces no visible change when it receives keyboard focus — no outline, border, background, or box-shadow shift is applied via :focus.
issue-an-xml-lang-attribute-is-present-but-has-an-empty-value-providing-no-language-in-170bf8 = An xml:lang attribute is present but has an empty value, providing no language information to consumers that read xml:lang.
issue-body-text-in-a-primarily-left-to-right-page-is-rendered-with-text-align-right-wh-29106d = Body text in a primarily left-to-right page is rendered with text-align: right, which disrupts the expected reading flow.
issue-body-text-is-rendered-with-text-align-justify-which-creates-uneven-word-spacing-d6aa36 = Body text is rendered with text-align: justify, which creates uneven word spacing. Dyslexic readers and users with cognitive disabilities often lose their place in justified text.
issue-css-sets-outline-none-on-an-interactive-element-without-supplying-any-replacemen-bed01f = CSS sets outline: none on an interactive element without supplying any replacement :focus indicator (no border, box-shadow, or background change).
issue-colour-related-css-properties-color-background-color-border-color-are-applied-vi-db693c = Colour-related CSS properties (color, background-color, border-color) are applied via inline style="..." on an HTML element, making it hard for users to override via custom or high-contrast stylesheets.
issue-colour-related-css-rules-are-defined-in-an-embedded-style-block-inside-the-html-65c400 = Colour-related CSS rules are defined in an embedded <style> block inside the HTML document rather than in an external stylesheet, making them harder for users to override.
issue-heading-levels-declared-in-the-dom-do-not-align-with-the-visual-size-hierarchy-f-963afd = Heading levels declared in the DOM do not align with the visual size hierarchy — for example, a visually larger heading carries a lower-priority level than a visually smaller one.
issue-headings-on-the-page-appear-in-an-illogical-sequence-for-example-a-higher-level-6ec269 = Headings on the page appear in an illogical sequence — for example, a higher-level heading (<h1> or <h2>) appears in the DOM after a lower-level one (<h3> or <h4>) under the same section.
issue-information-appears-to-be-conveyed-only-by-a-visual-property-colour-icon-positio-c23cd5 = Information appears to be conveyed only by a visual property (colour, icon position, shape, or font weight) without an accompanying text label or non-visual cue.
issue-more-than-one-h1-element-was-found-on-the-page-wcag-and-document-outline-best-pr-04eb11 = More than one <h1> element was found on the page. WCAG and document-outline best practice expect exactly one top-level heading per page.
issue-more-than-one-main-or-role-main-element-was-found-on-the-page-there-must-be-exac-c7034d = More than one <main> (or role="main") element was found on the page. There must be exactly one main landmark identifying the primary content.
issue-more-than-one-banner-landmark-was-found-at-the-top-level-of-the-page-the-aria-sp-8169e7 = More than one banner landmark was found at the top level of the page. The ARIA spec allows only a single banner landmark per page.
issue-more-than-one-contentinfo-landmark-was-found-at-the-top-level-of-the-page-the-ar-f25d62 = More than one contentinfo landmark was found at the top level of the page. The ARIA spec allows only a single contentinfo (footer) landmark per page.
issue-no-h1-h6-elements-and-no-elements-with-role-heading-were-found-anywhere-in-the-p-255aa1 = No <h1>–<h6> elements and no elements with role="heading" were found anywhere in the page's content.
issue-one-or-more-elements-use-an-inline-style-attribute-inline-styles-override-styles-6e91b5 = One or more elements use an inline style="..." attribute. Inline styles override stylesheets and can interfere with user style sheets, high-contrast modes, dark mode, or text-resizing adjustments.
issue-one-or-more-links-on-the-page-point-to-pdf-files-each-linked-pdf-requires-a-sepa-7d3941 = One or more links on the page point to .pdf files. Each linked PDF requires a separate accessibility audit, since the HTML scan cannot evaluate the contents of the PDF itself.
issue-pressing-tab-from-within-an-open-modal-allows-focus-to-escape-back-to-the-underl-43d28f = Pressing Tab from within an open modal allows focus to escape back to the underlying page content instead of cycling within the dialog.
issue-substantive-page-content-sits-outside-every-defined-landmark-banner-nav-main-com-8314df = Substantive page content sits outside every defined landmark (banner, nav, main, complementary, contentinfo, region, search, form). Screen reader users navigating by landmarks will skip past it.
issue-text-in-more-than-one-language-was-detected-on-the-page-but-the-secondary-langua-b00f2a = Text in more than one language was detected on the page, but the secondary-language passages are not wrapped in elements that carry a lang attribute.
issue-the-focus-styles-for-an-element-set-the-outline-or-other-indicator-to-a-transpar-abc138 = The :focus styles for an element set the outline (or other indicator) to a transparent or near-transparent colour, so focus is technically present but visually undetectable.
issue-the-html-element-has-a-lang-attribute-but-its-value-is-an-empty-string-lang-assi-0817c6 = The <html> element has a lang attribute, but its value is an empty string (lang=""). Assistive tech treats this as "no language declared".
issue-the-html-element-has-no-lang-attribute-so-assistive-tech-cannot-determine-the-pa-076109 = The <html> element has no lang attribute, so assistive tech cannot determine the page's primary language for pronunciation and translation.
issue-the-main-or-role-main-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attributes-66e5ee = The <main> (or role="main") element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set, even though only one labelling mechanism is needed.
issue-the-main-element-or-role-main-appears-nested-inside-another-landmark-such-as-nav-81dd1e = The <main> element (or role="main") appears nested inside another landmark such as <nav>, <aside>, or <header>. <main> must be a top-level landmark.
issue-the-main-element-has-tabindex-0-which-inserts-it-into-the-keyboard-tab-order-lan-e62e82 = The <main> element has tabindex="0", which inserts it into the keyboard tab order. Landmarks should not be tab stops themselves — at most they may use tabindex="-1" to receive programmatic focus.
issue-the-document-s-head-contains-no-title-element-so-browsers-screen-readers-and-boo-d3ab25 = The document's <head> contains no <title> element, so browsers, screen readers, and bookmark tools have no name for the page.
issue-the-element-has-both-a-lang-and-an-xml-lang-attribute-but-their-values-disagree-ddd150 = The element has both a lang and an xml:lang attribute, but their values disagree. The HTML spec requires them to match exactly when both are present.
issue-the-on-screen-reading-order-produced-by-the-visual-layout-differs-from-the-dom-s-5a4452 = The on-screen reading order produced by the visual layout differs from the DOM source order that screen readers and keyboard users follow.
issue-the-page-appears-to-have-a-footer-area-visually-copyright-secondary-links-but-no-c1d1bb = The page appears to have a footer area visually (copyright, secondary links) but no <footer> at the top level and no element with role="contentinfo".
issue-the-page-appears-to-have-a-header-area-visually-logo-top-navigation-but-no-heade-ebc813 = The page appears to have a header area visually (logo, top navigation) but no <header> at the top level and no element with role="banner".
issue-the-page-contains-no-h1-element-without-a-top-level-heading-there-is-no-machine-56c0af = The page contains no <h1> element. Without a top-level heading, there is no machine-readable label identifying the page's primary topic.
issue-the-page-contains-no-header-element-at-the-top-level-and-no-element-with-role-ba-1f093f = The page contains no <header> element at the top level and no element with role="banner", so the site header region is not exposed as a landmark.
issue-the-page-contains-no-main-element-and-no-element-with-role-main-so-there-is-no-m-de4256 = The page contains no <main> element and no element with role="main", so there is no machine-readable signal indicating where the primary content begins.
issue-the-page-contains-no-nav-elements-and-no-elements-with-role-navigation-so-screen-be6978 = The page contains no <nav> elements and no elements with role="navigation", so screen reader users cannot use landmark navigation to jump to a navigation region.
issue-the-page-has-more-than-one-banner-landmark-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-no-aria-7e580e = The page has more than one banner landmark, but at least one of them has no aria-label or aria-labelledby. All banners need labels when more than one exists.
issue-the-page-has-more-than-one-complementary-landmark-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-n-ac4c4d = The page has more than one complementary landmark, but at least one of them has no aria-label or aria-labelledby.
issue-the-page-has-more-than-one-contentinfo-landmark-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-no-252c9b = The page has more than one contentinfo landmark, but at least one of them has no aria-label or aria-labelledby.
issue-the-page-has-more-than-one-navigation-landmark-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-no-a-8a0591 = The page has more than one navigation landmark, but at least one of them has no aria-label or aria-labelledby to distinguish it.
issue-the-page-has-more-than-one-region-landmark-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-no-aria-b55bf4 = The page has more than one region landmark, but at least one of them has no aria-label or aria-labelledby. All regions need labels when more than one exists.
issue-the-page-has-no-footer-at-the-top-level-and-no-element-with-role-contentinfo-wit-def33d = The page has no <footer> at the top level and no element with role="contentinfo". Without a contentinfo landmark, screen reader users cannot quickly jump to the page footer.
issue-the-page-has-no-header-at-the-top-level-and-no-element-with-role-banner-without-f93c25 = The page has no <header> at the top level and no element with role="banner". Without a banner landmark, screen reader users cannot jump straight to the site header.
issue-the-page-has-no-element-with-role-main-and-no-main-element-identifying-the-prima-016a53 = The page has no element with role="main" and no <main> element identifying the primary content region.
issue-the-page-loads-or-executes-one-or-more-script-elements-verify-that-the-page-s-es-6a10ab = The page loads or executes one or more <script> elements. Verify that the page's essential functionality still works when JavaScript is disabled or fails to load.
issue-the-page-runs-animations-or-transitions-but-no-css-rules-respond-to-the-prefers-073137 = The page runs animations or transitions but no CSS rules respond to the prefers-reduced-motion media query, so users who have reduced-motion enabled still see full motion.
issue-the-primary-language-code-on-the-page-e-g-on-html-lang-is-structurally-malformed-6cabc9 = The primary language code on the page (e.g., on <html lang="...">) is structurally malformed — wrong number of characters, wrong case for a region subtag, or an invalid separator.
issue-the-primary-language-subtag-e-g-the-xx-in-lang-xx-ca-is-not-a-recognised-iso-639-361c8d = The primary language subtag (e.g., the "xx" in lang="xx-CA") is not a recognised ISO 639 language code.
issue-the-primary-language-subtag-inside-an-xml-lang-attribute-is-not-a-recognised-iso-7c8a0a = The primary language subtag inside an xml:lang attribute is not a recognised ISO 639 language code.
issue-the-region-subtag-inside-a-link-s-hreflang-attribute-is-not-a-recognised-iso-316-8877f3 = The region subtag inside a link's hreflang attribute is not a recognised ISO 3166-1 country code.
issue-the-region-subtag-inside-an-xml-lang-attribute-is-not-a-recognised-iso-3166-1-co-004404 = The region subtag inside an xml:lang attribute is not a recognised ISO 3166-1 country code.
issue-the-region-subtag-of-an-element-s-lang-attribute-e-g-the-zz-in-lang-en-zz-is-not-d007ab = The region subtag of an element's lang attribute (e.g., the "ZZ" in lang="en-ZZ") is not a recognised ISO 3166-1 country code.
issue-the-visual-size-weight-or-styling-of-headings-on-the-page-does-not-consistently-8ecd4a = The visual size, weight, or styling of headings on the page does not consistently match the underlying heading levels in the DOM. Sighted users perceive a different hierarchy than screen reader users do.
issue-time-based-content-countdown-auto-rotating-carousel-session-timer-is-running-on-e048b6 = Time-based content (countdown, auto-rotating carousel, session timer) is running on the page without user controls to pause, stop, or extend it.
issue-two-or-more-nav-elements-on-the-page-resolve-to-the-same-computed-accessible-nam-21edf2 = Two or more <nav> elements on the page resolve to the same computed accessible name, so screen readers cannot distinguish them when listing navigation landmarks.
issue-two-or-more-nav-elements-were-found-on-the-page-and-at-least-one-of-them-has-no-09bde3 = Two or more <nav> elements were found on the page, and at least one of them has no aria-label or aria-labelledby. Each nav landmark needs a label when there is more than one.
issue-two-or-more-nav-landmarks-share-the-same-accessible-name-e-g-both-labelled-main-f043a9 = Two or more <nav> landmarks share the same accessible name (e.g., both labelled "Main navigation"), so users cannot distinguish them in the landmarks list.
issue-two-or-more-banner-landmarks-on-the-page-share-the-same-accessible-name-so-scree-e54207 = Two or more banner landmarks on the page share the same accessible name, so screen reader users cannot distinguish between them in the landmarks list.
issue-two-or-more-complementary-landmarks-on-the-page-share-the-same-accessible-name-e-5890a2 = Two or more complementary landmarks on the page share the same accessible name. Each complementary region needs a unique label so users can tell them apart.
issue-two-or-more-contentinfo-footer-landmarks-on-the-page-share-the-same-accessible-n-2770d8 = Two or more contentinfo (footer) landmarks on the page share the same accessible name, making them indistinguishable in the landmarks list.
issue-two-or-more-form-landmarks-on-the-page-share-the-same-accessible-name-so-users-c-279ce9 = Two or more form landmarks on the page share the same accessible name, so users cannot tell from the landmarks list which form is which.
issue-two-or-more-region-landmarks-on-the-page-share-the-same-accessible-name-so-they-9831c6 = Two or more region landmarks on the page share the same accessible name, so they cannot be told apart in the landmarks list.
issue-two-or-more-search-landmarks-share-the-same-accessible-name-if-multiple-search-a-c5cafb = Two or more search landmarks share the same accessible name. If multiple search areas exist, each needs a unique label (e.g., "Site search", "Product search").
issue-visual-ai-analysis-flagged-this-element-as-a-likely-accessibility-problem-but-th-6030fb = Visual AI analysis flagged this element as a likely accessibility problem, but the specific failure mode wasn't matched to one of our catalogued issue types. The element's screenshot and surrounding context are preserved in the report so you can determine which WCAG criterion applies.
issue-visual-analysis-identified-a-modal-style-overlay-but-the-container-element-has-n-a0dd31 = Visual analysis identified a modal-style overlay, but the container element has no role="dialog" or role="alertdialog" attribute.
issue-when-the-element-receives-keyboard-focus-no-visible-change-occurs-no-outline-bor-9cede7 = When the element receives keyboard focus, no visible change occurs — no outline, border, background-colour, or box-shadow is applied.
issue-while-the-modal-is-open-tab-shift-tab-can-move-focus-to-elements-outside-the-dia-e98aaa = While the modal is open, Tab/Shift+Tab can move focus to elements outside the dialog instead of cycling through controls inside it.
issue-role-menu-or-role-menuitem-is-used-on-plain-navigation-links-the-menu-role-patte-2bb0af = role="menu" or role="menuitem" is used on plain navigation links. The menu role pattern is meant for application-style menus (with arrow-key navigation), not for ordinary site navigation lists.

# Regenerated by scripts/regenerate_inline_issue_ids.py — entries
# below cover newly-added catalog descriptions. Sort order is by FTL
# ID for review-friendliness; do not hand-edit unless you're also
