issue-a-fieldset-element-groups-related-controls-but-has-no-legend-child-so-the-groupi-d41376 = A <fieldset> element groups related controls but has no <legend> child, so the grouping has no accessible name describing what the contained fields collectively represent.
issue-a-form-element-exists-in-the-dom-but-contains-no-child-nodes-whatsoever-no-input-be3242 = A <form> element exists in the DOM but contains no child nodes whatsoever: no inputs, no buttons, no text, and no markup of any kind between its tags.
issue-a-form-element-has-an-aria-labelledby-attribute-but-either-the-attribute-value-i-04d833 = A <form> element has an aria-labelledby attribute, but either the attribute value is empty or the referenced element contains no text content, so the form's computed accessible name is blank.
issue-a-form-element-uses-the-title-attribute-as-its-sole-source-of-accessible-name-th-70af49 = A <form> element uses the title attribute as its sole source of accessible name. The title attribute is exposed inconsistently across browsers and assistive technologies, and it is unavailable to touch-only and mobile users who cannot hover.
issue-a-form-element-was-found-that-contains-no-recognizable-submit-control-there-is-n-f90638 = A <form> element was found that contains no recognizable submit control: there is no <button type="submit">, no <input type="submit">, and no <input type="image">. The form may instead rely on a scripted submit triggered by a <div>, a link, or the Enter key, which automated detection cannot confirm. Verify manually that the form can be submitted through an accessible, keyboard-operable control.
issue-a-form-element-s-aria-labelledby-contains-an-id-that-matches-no-element-anywhere-edee67 = A <form> element's aria-labelledby contains an id that matches no element anywhere on the page. The reference is broken, so the browser computes no accessible name from it.
issue-a-form-element-s-aria-labelledby-references-an-element-that-is-hidden-via-displa-f9b6d1 = A <form> element's aria-labelledby references an element that is hidden via display:none, visibility:hidden, or the hidden attribute. Although aria-labelledby can use hidden text for naming, relying on display:none/visibility:hidden content is fragile and the relationship is easily broken or removed.
issue-a-form-uses-aria-labelledby-to-reference-an-element-that-is-not-a-heading-h1-h6-c67a99 = A <form> uses aria-labelledby to reference an element that is not a heading (<h1>-<h6>). The form landmark is being named by text that is not the section heading introducing it.
issue-a-label-element-has-a-for-attribute-whose-value-does-not-match-the-id-of-any-ele-52368a = A <label> element has a for attribute whose value does not match the id of any element anywhere on the page. The label therefore points to nothing and is not associated with any form control.
issue-a-label-element-has-no-for-attribute-and-does-not-implicitly-contain-a-form-cont-3e8c75 = A <label> element has no for attribute and does not implicitly contain a form control inside it. The label is therefore not associated with any field and provides no programmatic name to a control.
issue-a-nav-element-or-element-with-role-navigation-is-contained-inside-another-naviga-3df112 = A <nav> element (or element with role="navigation") is contained inside another navigation landmark. The detected nav appears as a child of an outer nav, producing nested navigation landmarks.
issue-a-nav-landmark-was-found-that-has-neither-an-aria-label-nor-an-aria-labelledby-a-17fdb0 = A <nav> landmark was found that has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute, so it has no explicit accessible name. If the page contains more than one navigation region, this one cannot be distinguished from the others in the landmarks list.
issue-a-nav-landmark-s-accessible-name-for-example-main-navigation-contains-the-word-n-d842d5 = A <nav> landmark's accessible name (for example "Main navigation") contains the word "navigation". Screen readers already announce the role of this region as "navigation", so including that word in the label is redundant and does not describe what the navigation actually leads to.
issue-a-section-element-was-found-with-no-aria-label-aria-labelledby-or-title-attribut-59fb19 = A <section> element was found with no aria-label, aria-labelledby, or title attribute. Per the ARIA specification, a <section> only maps to the region landmark role when it has an accessible name, so this unlabelled section is not exposed as a landmark and will not appear in the landmarks list.
issue-a-style-block-was-found-embedded-in-the-page-rather-than-supplied-via-an-externa-2287f3 = A <style> block was found embedded in the page rather than supplied via an external stylesheet. This is a discovery notice: embedded styles cannot be overridden by user style sheets or browser extensions in the same way external CSS can.
issue-a-table-uses-th-header-cells-in-its-first-row-but-does-not-group-them-inside-a-t-32d08a = A <table> uses <th> header cells in its first row but does not group them inside a <thead> element, and the body rows are not wrapped in <tbody>. The header and data rows are siblings within the table rather than being grouped into distinct row sections.
issue-a-banner-landmark-a-top-level-header-element-or-an-element-with-role-banner-carr-edb2b3 = A banner landmark (a top-level <header> element, or an element with role="banner") carries an aria-label or aria-labelledby attribute whose computed value resolves to an empty string. The landmark therefore exposes an empty accessible name to assistive technology.
issue-a-banner-landmark-top-level-header-or-role-banner-is-rendered-inside-another-lan-ac12e2 = A banner landmark (top-level <header> or role="banner") is rendered inside another landmark region such as <main>, <nav>, or <aside>. The ARIA Landmark specification requires the banner to be a top-level region of the document and not contained within another landmark.
issue-a-banner-landmark-element-has-both-an-aria-label-and-an-aria-labelledby-attribut-3f2717 = A banner landmark element has both an aria-label and an aria-labelledby attribute set at the same time. Per the accessible name computation, aria-labelledby takes precedence and aria-label is ignored, but supplying both signals conflicting labelling intent.
issue-a-banner-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-banner-for-example-aria-la-919f9d = A banner landmark's accessible name contains the word "banner" (for example aria-label="Site banner"). Screen readers already announce the landmark's role as "banner", so including the word in the name repeats that role.
issue-a-block-of-running-body-text-is-rendered-with-text-align-right-or-dir-styling-th-107ccf = A block of running body text is rendered with text-align: right (or dir/styling that right-aligns it) on a page whose primary language reads left to right, so each line ends flush right and begins at a ragged left edge.
issue-a-button-toggles-content-open-and-closed-or-switches-a-setting-on-and-off-but-it-df4521 = A button toggles content open and closed or switches a setting on and off, but it does not expose its current state through aria-expanded or aria-pressed, so the state exists only visually.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-aside-or-role-complementary-is-contained-within-another-8c6fb6 = A complementary landmark (<aside> or role="complementary") is contained within another landmark element. The ARIA Landmark specification requires complementary regions to be top-level regions of the document, not nested inside banner, navigation, main, or other landmarks.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-an-aside-element-or-an-element-with-role-complementary-096dfd = A complementary landmark (an <aside> element or an element with role="complementary") exists with no aria-label or aria-labelledby, so it has no accessible name. If the page contains more than one complementary region, the unlabelled ones cannot be told apart.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-an-aside-element-or-an-element-with-role-complementary-240a76 = A complementary landmark (an <aside> element or an element with role="complementary") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby attribute whose computed value resolves to an empty string, leaving the landmark with no accessible name.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attribu-b85e98 = A complementary landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set simultaneously, even though only one labelling mechanism should be used. In the accessible name computation aria-labelledby wins and aria-label is ignored.
issue-a-complementary-landmark-s-accessible-name-contains-the-word-complementary-for-e-72379f = A complementary landmark's accessible name contains the word "complementary" (for example aria-label="Complementary content"). Screen readers already announce the landmark's role as "complementary", so the name duplicates the role.
issue-a-contentinfo-footer-landmark-was-detected-that-has-neither-an-aria-label-nor-an-b87d50 = A contentinfo (footer) landmark was detected that has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute, so it has no explicit accessible name. A page typically has only one contentinfo region, but an explicit label still helps screen reader users confirm what they have jumped to when navigating the landmark list.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-a-top-level-footer-element-or-an-element-with-role-conten-53d7c4 = A contentinfo landmark (a top-level <footer> element, or an element with role="contentinfo") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby attribute whose computed value resolves to an empty string, so the landmark has no accessible name.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-top-level-footer-or-role-contentinfo-is-rendered-inside-a-dc2b20 = A contentinfo landmark (top-level <footer> or role="contentinfo") is rendered inside another landmark such as <main> or <nav>. The ARIA Landmark specification disallows this: contentinfo must be a top-level region of the document.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-element-has-both-aria-label-and-aria-labelledby-attribute-d8da0a = A contentinfo landmark element has both aria-label and aria-labelledby attributes set at the same time. The accessible name computation gives precedence to aria-labelledby and ignores aria-label, so the duplication reflects confused authoring.
issue-a-contentinfo-landmark-s-accessible-name-set-via-aria-label-or-aria-labelledby-c-ab10af = A contentinfo landmark's accessible name (set via aria-label or aria-labelledby) contains the word "contentinfo". Screen readers already announce the role of this region, so including the role word in the label duplicates that information and exposes an internal technical term that means nothing to most users.
issue-a-continuously-looping-animation-runs-indefinitely-and-cannot-be-paused-stopped-1f5e9d = A continuously looping animation runs indefinitely and cannot be paused, stopped, or hidden.
issue-a-custom-interactive-control-is-built-without-the-aria-roles-and-states-needed-t-8942ec = A custom interactive control is built without the ARIA roles and states needed to describe it.
issue-a-custom-interactive-widget-such-as-a-tab-set-accordion-dropdown-or-menu-built-f-0f5dd0 = A custom interactive widget (such as a tab set, accordion, dropdown, or menu built from generic elements) was detected, but it carries none of the ARIA roles and states that describe what it is and how it behaves.
issue-a-dialog-has-the-dialog-role-but-is-not-given-an-accessible-name-bbb403 = A dialog has the dialog role but is not given an accessible name.
issue-a-digital-map-was-detected-on-the-page-along-with-metadata-about-its-provider-ty-930bac = A digital map was detected on the page, along with metadata about its provider, type, and any apparent accessibility features. This is a discovery notice for review, not a confirmed defect.
issue-a-field-s-aria-labelledby-references-an-element-that-is-not-a-label-nor-a-headin-f0368e = A field's aria-labelledby references an element that is not a <label> nor a heading-like or text-bearing element with a meaningful name (for example, it points to a generic <div> or an empty container with no role). The element supplies an unreliable or absent accessible name.
issue-a-field-s-computed-accessible-name-does-not-begin-with-or-contain-the-text-of-it-02140f = A field's computed accessible name does not begin with, or contain, the text of its visible label. The name announced to assistive technology and used by voice control differs from what a sighted user reads on screen.
issue-a-focus-indicator-exists-but-is-too-low-contrast-or-too-thin-to-be-clearly-seen-d78f62 = A focus indicator exists but is too low-contrast or too thin to be clearly seen against its surroundings.
issue-a-focus-indicator-is-defined-with-outline-offset-0-so-the-outline-sits-flush-aga-eaa544 = A focus indicator is defined with outline-offset: 0, so the outline sits flush against the element. Depending on the element's border and the surrounding colours, the focus ring can visually merge with the element edge and become hard to distinguish.
issue-a-focus-outline-is-supplied-through-css-but-no-outline-offset-is-declared-so-the-c2731d = A focus outline is supplied through CSS but no outline-offset is declared, so the outline is drawn flush against the element. Depending on the element's own border, padding, or background, the outline can be partially or fully obscured.
issue-a-form-field-carries-an-aria-label-attribute-whose-value-is-an-empty-string-aria-4c3815 = A form field carries an aria-label attribute whose value is an empty string (aria-label="" or only whitespace). Because aria-label, when present, overrides other naming sources, the field ends up with no accessible name at all even though it appears to be labelled.
issue-a-form-field-has-a-basic-label-but-nearby-content-instructions-formatting-requir-768b38 = A form field has a basic label, but nearby content (instructions, formatting requirements, units, or error text) appears related to the field and is not programmatically connected to it. The field could benefit from aria-labelledby for a composite name or aria-describedby for the supporting guidance.
issue-a-form-field-has-an-aria-labelledby-attribute-whose-value-is-empty-or-only-white-286577 = A form field has an aria-labelledby attribute whose value is empty or only whitespace, so it references no element. No accessible name is computed from it, leaving the field effectively unnamed.
issue-a-form-field-is-marked-mandatory-programmatically-the-required-attribute-or-aria-a91afe = A form field is marked mandatory programmatically (the required attribute or aria-required="true") but shows no visible "required" indicator near its label, so sighted users cannot tell the field must be completed before submission.
issue-a-form-field-uses-aria-label-to-provide-its-accessible-name-even-though-it-has-o-fb0a4e = A form field uses aria-label to provide its accessible name even though it has, or could reasonably have, a visible textual prompt that should be marked up as a real <label>. The aria-label hides the labelling from sighted users while satisfying only assistive technology.
issue-a-form-landmark-a-form-element-with-an-accessible-name-source-or-an-element-with-69b8d9 = A form landmark (a <form> element with an accessible name source, or an element with role="form") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby attribute that resolves to an empty string. The label was supplied but evaluates to nothing useful (for example aria-label="" or aria-labelledby pointing to an element that has no text).
issue-a-form-landmark-element-has-both-an-aria-label-attribute-and-an-aria-labelledby-b6dc65 = A form landmark element has both an aria-label attribute and an aria-labelledby attribute set at the same time. These are two competing ways to provide an accessible name, and only one should be used on a given element.
issue-a-heading-element-exists-in-the-dom-but-is-hidden-via-display-none-most-screen-r-a73efa = A heading element exists in the DOM but is hidden via display:none. Most screen readers skip display:none content, so the heading does not appear in the headings list or the accessibility tree.
issue-a-heading-s-coded-level-does-not-match-its-visual-hierarchy-a7169e = A heading's coded level does not match its visual hierarchy.
issue-a-landmark-contains-a-heading-at-or-near-its-start-that-could-naturally-name-the-8d593b = A landmark contains a heading at or near its start that could naturally name the region, but the landmark's aria-labelledby points to a different element instead of that heading. The visible heading and the programmatic label therefore come from two different sources.
issue-a-landmark-contains-a-heading-that-could-naturally-serve-as-its-accessible-name-6f853f = A landmark contains a heading that could naturally serve as its accessible name, but the landmark has no aria-labelledby pointing to that heading and no other accessible name. The descriptive heading text is present but not connected to the region programmatically.
issue-a-modal-dialog-is-currently-open-but-its-container-element-has-no-aria-label-no-543cde = A modal dialog is currently open, but its container element has no aria-label, no aria-labelledby pointing to a visible title, and no other source of an accessible name. The dialog is exposed to assistive technology with an empty name.
issue-a-modal-dialog-is-not-given-a-dialog-role-df7785 = A modal dialog is not given a dialog role.
issue-a-modal-dialog-is-open-but-contains-no-focusable-elements-at-all-no-buttons-no-l-150dab = A modal dialog is open but contains no focusable elements at all — no buttons, no links, and no form inputs. There is nothing inside the dialog that a keyboard user can move focus to.
issue-a-modal-dialog-overlay-is-displayed-but-its-container-does-not-carry-aria-modal-09a9e8 = A modal dialog overlay is displayed, but its container does not carry aria-modal="true". Without this attribute some assistive technologies may continue to expose the background page content as if it were still available.
issue-a-modal-dialog-was-detected-that-offers-no-visible-close-affordance-no-labelled-a67b44 = A modal dialog was detected that offers no visible close affordance — no labelled close button, no "X" control, and no Cancel or Done action. Nothing on screen tells the user how to leave the dialog.
issue-a-modal-has-no-visible-mechanism-to-close-it-1b964f = A modal has no visible mechanism to close it.
issue-a-navigation-landmark-a-nav-element-or-an-element-with-role-navigation-has-an-ar-d34b53 = A navigation landmark (a <nav> element or an element with role="navigation") has an aria-label or aria-labelledby attribute that resolves to an empty string. A labelling attribute is present but produces no text, so the nav has no usable accessible name.
issue-a-navigation-landmark-element-nav-or-role-navigation-has-both-an-aria-label-attr-b2c16e = A navigation landmark element (<nav> or role="navigation") has both an aria-label attribute and an aria-labelledby attribute set at the same time. These are two competing accessible-name mechanisms; only one should be used per element.
issue-a-navigation-menu-such-as-a-flyout-or-mega-menu-was-detected-without-the-appropr-e396b4 = A navigation menu (such as a flyout or mega-menu) was detected without the appropriate ARIA pattern: there is no menu/menuitem structure or navigation landmark, and no roving-tabindex keyboard handling for moving between items.
issue-a-non-interactive-element-such-as-div-span-or-p-has-tabindex-0-inserting-it-into-9ccc40 = A non-interactive element such as <div>, <span>, or <p> has tabindex="0", inserting it into the natural keyboard tab order even though it has no role, no keyboard handlers, and no apparent reason to receive focus.
issue-a-non-semantic-element-is-being-used-as-a-button-instead-of-a-real-button-32de4c = A non-semantic element is being used as a button instead of a real <button>.
issue-a-non-semantic-element-is-being-used-as-a-link-instead-of-a-real-a-href-7f584d = A non-semantic element is being used as a link instead of a real <a href>.
issue-a-piece-of-substantive-page-content-is-located-outside-all-landmark-regions-bann-9eb886 = A piece of substantive page content is located outside all landmark regions (banner, navigation, main, complementary, contentinfo, region, search, and form). It belongs to none of the page's defined regions.
issue-a-region-landmark-element-role-region-or-a-section-that-has-an-accessible-name-s-099f5e = A region landmark element (role="region", or a <section> that has an accessible-name source) has both an aria-label attribute and an aria-labelledby attribute set at the same time. Only one accessible-name mechanism should be used on the element.
issue-a-region-landmark-s-accessible-name-for-example-site-navigation-region-contains-222897 = A region landmark's accessible name (for example "Site navigation region") contains the word "navigation", even though this element is a region and not a navigation landmark. The label implies a navigation role that the element does not actually have.
issue-a-site-navigation-region-does-not-mark-which-item-corresponds-to-the-page-the-us-c692e2 = A site navigation region does not mark which item corresponds to the page the user is currently viewing. Note: this check is deprecated and has been split into ErrNoCurrentPageIndicatorScreenReader (no programmatic indicator such as aria-current) and ErrNoCurrentPageIndicatorMagnification (no sufficient visual indicator); use those codes instead.
issue-a-substantial-block-of-running-text-for-example-a-paragraph-or-longer-is-rendere-31a70b = A substantial block of running text (for example a paragraph or longer) is rendered in italics, using <i>, <em>, or a CSS font-style: italic rule applied to body-level content rather than to a short phrase.
issue-a-tabindex-attribute-is-set-on-a-non-interactive-element-such-as-div-p-or-sectio-980e3c = A tabindex attribute is set on a non-interactive element such as <div>, <p>, or <section> that has no ARIA role and no keyboard event handler. Focus therefore lands on an element that performs no action and exposes no control.
issue-a-video-or-audio-element-begins-playing-automatically-when-the-page-loads-and-no-de142c = A video or audio element begins playing automatically when the page loads, and no visible button or control to pause, stop, or mute it is present within the first few seconds of playback.
issue-ai-analysis-of-the-rendered-page-detected-a-heading-related-accessibility-issue-974ef8 = AI analysis of the rendered page detected a heading-related accessibility issue, such as a missing, mislabeled, or out-of-order heading that the DOM-only checks did not flag.
issue-an-animation-was-detected-whose-speed-and-contrast-changes-could-produce-rapid-f-79c86a = An animation was detected whose speed and contrast changes could produce rapid flashing or strobing that approaches or exceeds the seizure-risk threshold.
issue-an-element-behaves-like-a-clickable-control-it-has-a-click-handler-or-an-interac-747eae = An element behaves like a clickable control — it has a click handler or an interactive role — but its CSS does not set cursor: pointer, so the mouse cursor stays a default arrow and gives no hover affordance that the element can be activated.
issue-an-element-carries-an-aria-level-attribute-but-has-no-role-attribute-at-all-aria-1cc734 = An element carries an aria-level attribute but has no role attribute at all. aria-level is only meaningful when paired with role="heading".
issue-an-element-exposing-role-dialog-was-found-but-it-has-neither-an-aria-label-nor-a-d45135 = An element exposing role="dialog" was found, but it has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute, and no other mechanism (such as a referenced visible heading) supplies an accessible name. The dialog therefore reaches assistive technology with an empty name.
issue-an-element-has-a-title-attribute-but-its-value-is-empty-title-so-it-provides-no-acd137 = An element has a title attribute, but its value is empty (title=""), so it provides no tooltip text and no fallback accessible name.
issue-an-element-has-an-aria-level-attribute-but-its-role-is-not-heading-and-it-is-not-4c7523 = An element has an aria-level attribute, but its role is not "heading" and it is not a native <h1>-<h6>. aria-level only has meaning on heading-role elements.
issue-an-element-has-an-onclick-handler-or-similar-javascript-click-listener-but-no-ro-68bd5f = An element has an onclick handler (or similar JavaScript click listener) but no role, no tabindex, and no keyboard event handlers, so it can be clicked but not activated with a keyboard.
issue-an-element-has-role-heading-but-no-aria-level-attribute-without-aria-level-assis-7a4239 = An element has role="heading" but no aria-level attribute. Without aria-level, assistive technology cannot determine the heading's place in the hierarchy.
issue-an-element-responds-to-mouse-clicks-but-cannot-be-reached-or-focused-using-the-k-973a50 = An element responds to mouse clicks but cannot be reached or focused using the keyboard.
issue-an-element-that-serves-as-the-destination-of-an-in-page-anchor-link-has-a-tabind-32103a = An element that serves as the destination of an in-page anchor link has a tabindex attribute set even though it is not itself an interactive control. Modern browsers move focus to anchor targets without requiring tabindex.
issue-an-element-uses-a-tabindex-value-above-10-which-signals-a-manually-orchestrated-4c5a81 = An element uses a tabindex value above 10, which signals a manually orchestrated tab sequence. Any positive tabindex pulls the element ahead of all elements with tabindex="0" or none, and large values usually mean a hand-numbered order that is fragile and easy to break when the page changes.
issue-an-element-with-role-region-was-found-that-is-missing-both-aria-label-and-aria-l-0be36d = An element with role="region" was found that is missing both aria-label and aria-labelledby, so it has no accessible name. An element with role="region" requires an accessible name to be exposed as a landmark, so without one it cannot be identified or distinguished in the landmarks list.
issue-an-element-s-aria-level-value-is-outside-the-valid-heading-range-values-must-be-5e3281 = An element's aria-level value is outside the valid heading range; values must be integers from 1 to 6.
issue-an-element-s-computed-accessible-name-resolves-to-a-generic-non-descriptive-term-d72b24 = An element's computed accessible name resolves to a generic, non-descriptive term such as "link", "button", "image", "click here", or "read more" rather than text that conveys the element's specific function or destination. The name may come from the element's text content, an aria-label, aria-labelledby, alt text, or a title attribute.
issue-an-element-s-lang-attribute-includes-a-region-subtag-that-is-not-a-valid-iso-316-503c1d = An element's lang attribute includes a region subtag that is not a valid ISO 3166-1 country code — for example the "ZZ" in lang="en-ZZ". The language part may be valid, but the region qualifier after the hyphen is not recognised.
issue-an-hreflang-attribute-was-found-on-an-element-that-is-not-an-a-area-or-link-the-42a231 = An hreflang attribute was found on an element that is not an <a>, <area>, or <link>. The hreflang attribute is only meaningful on link elements.
issue-an-interactive-element-carries-a-negative-tabindex-such-as-tabindex-1-the-elemen-1db0fc = An interactive element carries a negative tabindex such as tabindex="-1". The element stays visible and clickable with a mouse, but the negative value removes it from the sequential keyboard tab order so Tab will skip past it.
issue-an-interactive-element-does-not-declare-an-aria-role-describing-what-it-is-a33ded = An interactive element does not declare an ARIA role describing what it is.
issue-an-interactive-element-such-as-a-link-or-button-has-a-negative-tabindex-like-tab-724a75 = An interactive element such as a link or button has a negative tabindex like tabindex="-1". This is legitimate in some patterns (focus management in modals, roving tabindex in composite widgets) but frequently signals that a control was unintentionally removed from keyboard navigation.
issue-an-interactive-element-such-as-a-custom-widget-carries-a-tabindex-value-that-con-ca083f = An interactive element, such as a custom widget, carries a tabindex value that conflicts with how it must behave — for example tabindex="-1" on a control the user is expected to be able to Tab to, or a positive value that reorders it away from its visual position.
issue-an-open-modal-does-not-keep-keyboard-focus-inside-the-dialog-8ed228 = An open modal does not keep keyboard focus inside the dialog.
issue-an-xml-lang-attribute-is-present-on-an-element-but-has-an-empty-value-providing-e0efe6 = An xml:lang attribute is present on an element but has an empty value, providing no language information to consumers that read xml:lang.
issue-automatically-playing-media-starts-on-its-own-and-offers-no-visible-way-to-pause-6deeb3 = Automatically playing media starts on its own and offers no visible way to pause, stop, or mute it.
issue-background-content-behind-a-modal-is-not-made-inert-0b6d72 = Background content behind a modal is not made inert.
issue-content-appears-to-flash-or-strobe-rapidly-enough-to-be-a-potential-seizure-risk-666684 = Content appears to flash or strobe rapidly enough to be a potential seizure risk.
issue-content-that-appears-to-form-a-group-visually-for-example-a-label-and-its-value-b47dcd = Content that appears to form a group visually (for example, a label and its value, or a card and its caption) is separated in the DOM order or lacks any programmatic relationship tying the parts together.
issue-information-appears-to-be-conveyed-only-by-a-visual-property-colour-icon-positio-494fd6 = Information appears to be conveyed only by a visual property (colour, icon position, shape, or font weight) without an accompanying text label or other non-visual cue.
issue-items-that-look-grouped-on-screen-are-not-grouped-or-associated-in-the-markup-df5e2e = Items that look grouped on screen are not grouped or associated in the markup.
issue-more-than-one-banner-landmark-was-detected-at-the-top-level-of-the-page-a-banner-d19429 = More than one banner landmark was detected at the top level of the page. A banner landmark is created by a <header> element that is not nested inside <article>, <aside>, <main>, <nav>, or <section>, or by an element with role="banner". The ARIA model expects at most one banner landmark per page.
issue-more-than-one-banner-landmark-was-found-on-the-page-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-2336f9 = More than one banner landmark was found on the page, but at least one of them has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute. When more than one landmark of the same role exists, each instance needs a unique accessible name to be distinguishable.
issue-more-than-one-complementary-landmark-such-as-aside-or-role-complementary-was-fou-b4e4e9 = More than one complementary landmark (such as <aside> or role="complementary") was found on the page, but at least one of them has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute. With multiple landmarks of the same role, each needs a unique accessible name.
issue-more-than-one-contentinfo-landmark-was-detected-at-the-top-level-of-the-page-a-c-3ce0da = More than one contentinfo landmark was detected at the top level of the page. A contentinfo landmark is created by a <footer> element that is not nested inside <article>, <aside>, <main>, <nav>, or <section>, or by an element with role="contentinfo". The ARIA model expects at most one contentinfo landmark per page.
issue-more-than-one-contentinfo-landmark-was-found-on-the-page-but-at-least-one-of-the-902a39 = More than one contentinfo landmark was found on the page, but at least one of them has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute. When multiple landmarks of the same role exist, each instance needs a unique accessible name.
issue-more-than-one-navigation-landmark-nav-or-role-navigation-was-found-on-the-page-b-96aa97 = More than one navigation landmark (<nav> or role="navigation") was found on the page, but at least one of them has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute to distinguish it from the others.
issue-more-than-one-region-landmark-was-found-on-the-page-but-at-least-one-of-them-has-40e267 = More than one region landmark was found on the page, but at least one of them has neither an aria-label nor an aria-labelledby attribute. A <section> or role="region" element only becomes an exposed landmark when it has an accessible name, so an unlabelled one is dropped from landmark navigation.
issue-one-or-more-css-animations-or-transitions-were-detected-but-the-stylesheet-conta-53da3a = One or more CSS animations or transitions were detected, but the stylesheet contains no @media (prefers-reduced-motion) query to disable or tone them down for users who have requested reduced motion.
issue-one-or-more-elements-use-an-inline-style-attribute-this-is-a-discovery-notice-in-6029ed = One or more elements use an inline style="..." attribute. This is a discovery notice: inline styles override stylesheets and can interfere with user style sheets, high-contrast modes, dark mode, or text-resizing adjustments.
issue-page-content-was-found-that-is-not-contained-within-any-landmark-region-such-as-8c5f3f = Page content was found that is not contained within any landmark region such as banner/header, navigation, main, contentinfo/footer, or complementary/aside. Note: this check is deprecated and superseded by ErrContentOutsideLandmarks; new findings should be reported under that code.
issue-pressing-tab-from-within-an-open-modal-allows-focus-to-escape-back-to-the-underl-d0c0ce = Pressing Tab from within an open modal allows focus to escape back to the underlying page content instead of cycling among the focusable elements within the dialog. The modal does not implement a focus trap.
issue-text-in-more-than-one-language-was-detected-on-the-page-but-the-secondary-langua-aee7bc = Text in more than one language was detected on the page, but the secondary-language passages are not wrapped in elements that carry a lang attribute identifying their language.
issue-text-is-styled-to-look-like-a-heading-but-is-not-marked-up-with-a-heading-elemen-f3ed4e = Text is styled to look like a heading but is not marked up with a heading element.
issue-the-html-element-on-this-page-does-not-carry-a-lang-attribute-so-no-default-huma-cdc566 = The <html> element on this page does not carry a lang attribute, so no default human language is declared for the document.
issue-the-main-element-or-an-element-with-role-main-has-both-an-aria-label-attribute-a-0080c6 = The <main> element (or an element with role="main") has both an aria-label attribute and an aria-labelledby attribute set simultaneously. Only one accessible-name mechanism should be applied to the element.
issue-the-main-element-or-an-element-with-role-main-is-contained-within-another-landma-d89aa6 = The <main> element (or an element with role="main") is contained within another landmark region such as <nav>, <aside>, <header>/role="banner", <footer>/role="contentinfo", or another landmark. The main landmark must be a top-level region and cannot be a descendant of another landmark.
issue-the-main-element-has-tabindex-0-which-inserts-the-landmark-container-itself-into-5d1470 = The <main> element has tabindex="0", which inserts the landmark container itself into the sequential keyboard tab order. Landmark containers are not meant to be tab stops; at most they may carry tabindex="-1" so script can move focus to them programmatically (for example from a skip link).
issue-the-declared-page-language-does-not-match-the-language-of-the-visible-content-44883a = The declared page language does not match the language of the visible content.
issue-the-document-has-no-declared-default-human-language-0184b0 = The document has no declared default human language.
issue-the-document-skips-one-or-more-heading-levels-in-its-hierarchy-a2167d = The document skips one or more heading levels in its hierarchy.
issue-the-element-has-a-javascript-click-handler-that-triggers-an-action-but-it-is-not-8521fa = The element has a JavaScript click handler that triggers an action, but it is not in the keyboard tab order: it is a non-interactive element (such as a div or span) with no tabindex and no native focusability.
issue-the-element-has-both-a-lang-and-an-xml-lang-attribute-but-their-values-disagree-4fbfea = The element has both a lang and an xml:lang attribute, but their values disagree. The HTML specification requires them to match exactly when both are present.
issue-the-on-screen-reading-order-produced-by-the-visual-layout-for-example-reposition-72d93a = The on-screen reading order produced by the visual layout (for example, repositioned with CSS flexbox order, grid placement, floats, or absolute positioning) differs from the DOM source order that screen readers and keyboard navigation follow.
issue-the-page-contains-a-heading-structure-problem-identified-through-visual-analysis-b68329 = The page contains a heading structure problem identified through visual analysis.
issue-the-page-contains-more-than-one-complementary-landmark-and-at-least-two-of-them-810c72 = The page contains more than one complementary landmark and at least two of them have an identical accessible name, so they cannot be told apart in the landmarks list.
issue-the-page-contains-more-than-one-form-landmark-and-at-least-two-of-them-have-the-1596ba = The page contains more than one form landmark and at least two of them have the same accessible name, so users cannot tell from the landmarks list which form each entry corresponds to.
issue-the-page-contains-more-than-one-region-landmark-an-element-with-role-region-or-a-3a6bfc = The page contains more than one region landmark (an element with role="region", or a <section> with an accessible name) and at least two of them have an identical accessible name, so they cannot be told apart in the landmarks list.
issue-the-page-exposes-more-than-one-banner-landmark-and-at-least-two-of-them-have-the-788976 = The page exposes more than one banner landmark and at least two of them have the same accessible name. In the screen reader's landmarks list they appear as identical entries.
issue-the-page-exposes-more-than-one-contentinfo-footer-landmark-and-at-least-two-of-t-ffd24a = The page exposes more than one contentinfo (footer) landmark and at least two of them have the same accessible name, making them indistinguishable in the landmarks list.
issue-the-page-exposes-more-than-one-search-landmark-role-search-or-the-search-element-564b62 = The page exposes more than one search landmark (role="search" or the <search> element) and at least two share the same accessible name, so they cannot be distinguished in the landmarks list.
issue-the-page-loads-or-executes-one-or-more-script-elements-this-is-a-discovery-notic-a2b9fe = The page loads or executes one or more <script> elements. This is a discovery notice, not a defect: it flags that scripting is in use so a reviewer can verify the page degrades gracefully.
issue-the-page-visually-presents-a-footer-area-such-as-copyright-notices-legal-text-or-81b326 = The page visually presents a footer area (such as copyright notices, legal text, or secondary links) but has no top-level <footer> element and no element with role="contentinfo", so this content is not exposed as a contentinfo landmark.
issue-the-page-visually-presents-a-header-area-such-as-a-logo-site-title-or-top-level-e89c7a = The page visually presents a header area (such as a logo, site title, or top-level navigation) but has no top-level <header> element and no element with role="banner", so this content is not exposed as a banner landmark.
issue-the-primary-language-code-on-the-page-for-example-on-html-lang-is-structurally-m-10c7ab = The primary language code on the page (for example on <html lang="...">) is structurally malformed, with the wrong number of characters, wrong case for a region subtag, or an invalid separator.
issue-the-primary-language-subtag-for-example-the-xx-in-lang-xx-ca-is-not-a-recognised-f3d789 = The primary language subtag (for example the "xx" in lang="xx-CA") is not a recognised ISO 639 language code.
issue-the-region-country-subtag-in-the-page-s-primary-language-declaration-the-lang-at-909cea = The region (country) subtag in the page's primary language declaration (the lang attribute, e.g. on <html>) is not a recognised ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, for example lang="en-XY". The language part may be valid, but the region qualifier after the hyphen is not.
issue-the-region-country-subtag-inside-a-link-s-hreflang-attribute-is-not-a-valid-iso-59ff2e = The region (country) subtag inside a link's hreflang attribute is not a valid ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code. For example, a link declares hreflang="en-XY" where "XY" is not an assigned country code.
issue-the-region-country-subtag-inside-an-xml-lang-attribute-is-not-a-recognised-iso-3-581a8b = The region (country) subtag inside an xml:lang attribute is not a recognised ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, for example xml:lang="en-XY". The language portion may be valid, but the region qualifier after the hyphen is not assigned.
issue-the-site-animates-content-but-never-checks-whether-the-user-has-asked-their-syst-83a6de = The site animates content but never checks whether the user has asked their system to reduce motion.
issue-two-or-more-nav-navigation-landmarks-have-the-same-accessible-name-for-example-b-704c4e = Two or more <nav> (navigation) landmarks have the same accessible name — for example both labelled "Main navigation" — so they appear as identical entries in the landmarks list.
issue-visual-analysis-detected-an-interactive-element-that-produces-no-perceptible-vis-01fca8 = Visual analysis detected an interactive element that produces no perceptible visual change when it receives keyboard focus. No outline, border, background-colour, or box-shadow is applied on focus, so the focused state is indistinguishable from the unfocused state.
issue-visual-analysis-found-that-an-interactive-element-does-change-appearance-on-keyb-65019e = Visual analysis found that an interactive element does change appearance on keyboard focus, but the change is very subtle — for example a 1px low-contrast outline or a barely-shifted background — so the focused state is hard to distinguish from neighbouring elements.
issue-visual-analysis-identified-an-overlay-that-behaves-like-a-modal-dialog-centred-p-cda99e = Visual analysis identified an overlay that behaves like a modal dialog (centred panel over a dimmed backdrop), but the container element carries no role="dialog" or role="alertdialog" attribute, and it is not a native <dialog> element. Assistive technology sees only a generic block of content.
issue-while-the-modal-dialog-is-open-the-content-behind-it-appears-to-remain-interacti-a6bb63 = While the modal dialog is open, the content behind it appears to remain interactive — links, buttons, and form fields in the background are not disabled, hidden from assistive technology, or marked inert.
issue-while-the-modal-is-open-pressing-tab-or-shift-tab-can-move-focus-to-elements-out-b87fec = While the modal is open, pressing Tab or Shift+Tab can move focus to elements outside the dialog rather than cycling through the controls inside it. Focus is not confined to the modal as it should be.
